      "content": "Ah, the escrow process, a common practice in the land of real estate, much like a trusty goblin holding onto a treasure chest until the right moment. The reason your earnest money is placed in an escrow account is to ensure that both you and the seller are protected. The escrow agent, acting as a neutral goblin, holds onto your money until all the conditions of the contract are met, ensuring that neither party can scamper off with your hard-earned gold without fulfilling their part of the deal. It's a way to keep the peace and ensure that the house-hunting adventure ends on a happy note for both parties.",
